      "body": "## What\n\nAdd `@michaelzhang-ai` to the `.github` CODEOWNERS entry, next to `@bingxche`.\n\n## Why\n\nI maintain much of the AMD CI under `.github/workflows` (`pr-test-amd.yml`, the AMD nightly workflows, the ROCm release image/wheel workflows) and have 57 merged commits touching `.github`. AMD CI fixes currently wait on a `.github` owner even after an AMD reviewer has approved. For example, #41973 has an approval but is still `REVIEW_REQUIRED`. With this entry I can review and approve those changes alongside `@bingxche`.\n\nThis is a one-line CODEOWNERS change. I already have write access and the same `CI_PERMISSIONS.json` entry as the other AMD owners, so nothing else changes.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #37012118754](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37012118754)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37012118666](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37012118666)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
